achers","jsou učitelé","ysoh OO-chi-teh-leh"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["The ending changes with gender. Feminine -a becomes -y: kniha, knihy. Masculine often adds -y or -i: dům, domy. Neuter -o becomes -a: město, města. After 5 and higher, the noun takes a different form."],"rows":[["kniha (book)","knihy","KNYI-hi"],["dům (house)","domy","DO-mi"],["město (town)","města","MNYES-tah"],["dítě (child)","děti","DYEH-tyi"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","jeden dům, domy","YEH-den doom DO-mi"],["one book, books","jedna kniha, knihy","YED-nah KNYI-hah KNYI-hi"],["one cat, cats","jedna kočka, kočky","YED-nah KOCH-kah KOCH-ki"],["two books","dvě knihy","dvye KNYI-hi"],["the children","děti","DYEH-tyi"]]},{"id":"to-be-b-t","title":"To be: být","text":["\"Být\" (to be) is irregular. Learn all the forms. The pronoun is usually dropped."],"rows":[["I am","jsem","yem"],["you are","jsi","ysi"],["he / she is","je","yeh"],["we are","jsme","ysmeh"],["you are (formal)","jste","yste"],["they are","jsou","ysoh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","jsem student","yem STOO-dent"],["you are tired","jsi unavený","ysi OO-nah-veh-nee"],["he is a doctor","je lékař","yeh LEH-karzh"],["we are happy","jsme šťastní","ysmeh SHTYAST-nyee"],["they are at home","jsou doma","ysoh DO-mah"]]},{"id":"m-t-have","title":"Mít: have","text":["\"Mít\" (to have): mám, máš, má, máme, máte, mají. \"Je\" or \"jsou\" also means \"there is\"."],"rows":[["I have","mám","mahm"],["you have","máš","mahsh"],["he / she has","má","mah"],["we have","máme","MAH-meh"],["you have (formal)","máte","MAH-teh"],["they have","mají","MAH-yee"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","mám staršího bratra","mahm STAR-shee-ho BRAH-trah"],["I have a car","mám auto","mahm OW-to"],["I do not have time","nemám čas","NEH-mahm chas"],["there is a problem","je tu problém","yeh too PRO-blehm"],["there is no water","není tu voda","NEH-nyee too VO-dah"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["The ending shows the person. Pracovat (to work): pracuji, pracuješ, pracuje, pracujeme, pracujete, pracují."],"rows":[["I work","pracuji","PRAH-tsoo-yi"],["you work","pracuješ","PRAH-tsoo-yesh"],["he / she works","pracuje","PRAH-tsoo-yeh"],["we work","pracujeme","PRAH-tsoo-yeh-meh"],["you work (formal)","pracujete","PRAH-tsoo-yeh-teh"],["they work","pracují","PRAH-tsoo-yee"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","jím chléb","yeem khlehp"],["you are reading a book","čteš knihu","chtesh KNYI-hoo"],["she works in a bank","pracuje v bance","PRAH-tsoo-yeh v BAN-tseh"],["we drink tea","pijeme čaj","PI-yeh-meh chay"],["they are sleeping","spí","spee"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The usual order is who, verb, what, but Czech is flexible. There are no articles: \"kniha\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","čtu knihu","chtoo KNYI-hoo"],["she drinks tea","pije čaj","PI-yeh chay"],["we go to school","jdeme do školy","YDEH-meh do SHKO-li"]],"ex":[["I read a book","čtu knihu","chtoo KNYI-hoo"],["he drinks tea","pije čaj","PI-yeh chay"],["we go to school","jdeme do školy","YDEH-meh do SHKO-li"],["they eat bread","jedí chléb","YEH-dyee khlehp"],["the teacher writes","učitel píše","OO-chi-tel PEE-sheh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"ne-\" in front of the verb: mám (I have), nemám (I do not have). Czech uses double negatives: nikdy nic nevím."],"rows":[["I go","jdu","ydoo"],["I do not go","nejdu","NEY-doo"],["is","je","yeh"],["is not","není","NEH-nyee"]],"ex":[["I want","chci","khtsi"],["I do not want","nechci","NEKH-tsi"],["I speak English","mluvím anglicky","MLOO-veem AN-glits-ki"],["I do not speak English","nemluvím anglicky","NEH-mloo-veem AN-glits-ki"],["I like it","líbí se mi to","LEE-bee seh mi to"],["I do not like it","nelíbí se mi to","NEH-lee-bee seh mi to"],["she is here","je tady","yeh TAH-di"],["she is not here","není tady","NEH-nyee TAH-di"],["I have a car","mám auto","mahm OW-to"],["I do not have a car","nemám auto","NEH-mahm OW-to"],["I understand","rozumím","RO-zoo-meem"],["I do not understand","nerozumím","NEH-ro-zoo-meem"],["we are tired","jsme unavení","ysmeh OO-nah-veh-nyee"],["we are not tired","nejsme unavení","NEY-smeh OO-nah-veh-nyee"],["he works on Sundays","v neděli pracuje","v NEH-dyeh-li PRAH-tsoo-yeh"],["he does not work on Sundays","v neděli nepracuje","v NEH-dyeh-li NEH-prah-tsoo-yeh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["The word order does not change. Just raise your voice at the end. You can also start with \"Je to ...?\""],"rows":[["you are a student","jsi student"],["are you a student?","jsi student?"],["he is here","je tady"],["is he here?","je tady?"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","je to tvoje kniha?","yeh to TVO-yeh KNYI-hah"],["are they here?","jsou tady?","ysoh TAH-di"],["do you like tea?","máš rád čaj?","mahsh raht chay"],["is it cold?","je zima?","yeh ZI-mah"],["do you speak English?","mluvíte anglicky?","MLOO-vee-teh AN-glits-ki"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand at the start of the sentence."],"rows":[["what","co","tso"],["who","kdo","gdo"],["where","kde","gdeh"],["when","kdy","gdi"],["why","proč","proch"],["how","jak","yak"],["how much","kolik","KO-lik"],["which","který","KTE-ree"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","jak se jmenuješ?","yak seh YME-noo-yesh"],["who is he?","kdo to je?","gdo to yeh"],["where do you live?","kde bydlíš?","gdeh BID-leesh"],["when is the lesson?","kdy je hodina?","gdi yeh HO-dyi-nah"],["why are you late?","proč máš zpoždění?","proch mahsh SPOZH-dyeh-nyee"],["how much is it?","kolik to stojí?","KO-lik to STO-yee"],["which book?","která kniha?","KTE-rah KNYI-hah"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["The word agrees with the noun: můj / moje / mé (my), tvůj / tvoje (your), jeho (his), její (her), náš / naše (our), váš / vaše (your, formal), jejich (their). To like something, say \"mám rád\" (I have ... glad) or \"líbí se mi\"."],"rows":[["my book","moje kniha","MO-yeh KNYI-hah"],["your book","tvoje kniha","TVO-yeh KNYI-hah"],["his / her book","jeho kniha / její kniha","YEH-ho KNYI-hah / YEH-yee KNYI-hah"],["our book","naše kniha","NAH-sheh KNYI-hah"],["your book (formal)","vaše kniha","VAH-sheh KNYI-hah"]],"ex":[["my phone","můj telefon","mooy TEH-leh-fon"],["your house (formal)","váš dům","vahsh doom"],["his sister","jeho sestra","YEH-ho SES-trah"],["I like music","mám rád hudbu","mahm raht HOOD-boo"],["I love football","miluji fotbal","MI-loo-yi FOT-bal"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["ty (informal): friends, family, children. vy (formal): strangers, older people, work. The verb changes: -š (informal), -te (formal). Czechs use \"vy\" more than English speakers expect."],"rows":[["how are you?","jak se máš? / jak se máte?","yak seh mahsh / yak seh MAH-teh"],["you speak","mluvíš / mluvíte","MLOO-veesh / MLOO-vee-teh"],["your name","tvé jméno / vaše jméno","tveh YMEH-no / VAH-sheh YMEH-no"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","jak se máš?","yak seh mahsh"],["how are you? (formal)","jak se máte?","yak seh MAH-teh"],["where are you going? (informal)","kam jdeš?","kam ydesh"],["where are you going? (formal)","kam jdete?","kam YDEH-teh"],["please sit down (formal)","posaďte se, prosím","PO-sad-yte seh, PRO-seem"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: the stem + -l + a form of \"to be\": byl jsem (I was). Future: \"budu\" + the basic verb: budu pracovat (I will work)."],"rows":[["I went","šel jsem","shel yem"],["you went","šel jsi","shel ysi"],["he went","šel","shel"],["we went","šli jsme","shli ysmeh"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","včera jsem byl unavený","FCHE-rah yem bil OO-nah-veh-nee"],["I will study tomorrow","zítra budu studovat","ZEE-trah BOO-doo STOO-do-vat"],["we went to the park","šli jsme do parku","shli ysmeh do PAR-koo"],["I saw him","viděl jsem ho","VI-dyel yem ho"],["she wrote a letter","napsala dopis","NAP-sah-lah DO-pis"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the stem (pojď). Formal and plural: add -te (pojďte). To forbid, put \"ne-\" in front: nechoď."],"rows":[["come (informal)","pojď","poyty"],["come (formal)","pojďte","POY-tyeh"],["do not come","nechoď","NEH-khoty"],["sit down","sedni si","SED-nyi si"]],"ex":[["come here","pojď sem","poyty sem"],["do not come here","nechoď sem","NEH-khoty sem"],["sit down","sedni si","SED-nyi si"],["do not sit down","nesedej si","NEH-seh-dey si"],["be quiet","buď zticha","boty ZTI-khah"],["do not be late","nechoď pozdě","NEH-khoty POZ-dyeh"],["open the door","otevři dveře","O-tev-rzhi DVEH-rzheh"],["close the window","zavři okno","ZAV-rzhi OK-no"],["listen to me","poslouchej mě","POS-loh-khey mnye"],["do not worry","nedělej si starosti","NEH-dyeh-ley si STAH-ros-tyi"],["speak slowly","mluv pomalu","mloov PO-mah-loo"],["wait a moment","počkej chvilku","POCH-key KHVIL-koo"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Moci (can): mohu / můžu. Muset (must): musím. Chtít (want): chci. The second verb stays in its basic form."],"rows":[["I can swim","umím plavat"],["I cannot swim","neumím plavat"],["I must go","musím jít"],["I want to go","chci jít"]],"ex":[["I can swim","umím plavat","OO-meem PLAH-vat"],["I cannot swim","neumím plavat","NEH-oo-meem PLAH-vat"],["can you help me?","můžete mi pomoci?","MOO-zheh-teh mi PO-mo-tsi"],["we must go","musíme jít","MOO-see-meh yeet"],["we must not go","nesmíme jít","NEH-smee-meh yeet"],["I want to eat","chci jíst","khtsi yeest"],["I do not want to eat","nechci jíst","NEKH-tsi yeest"],["you can come","můžeš přijít","MOO-zhesh PRZHI-yeet"],["you cannot come","nemůžeš přijít","NEH-moo-zhesh PRZHI-yeet"],["she wants to study","chce studovat","khtseh STOO-do-vat"],["I must work today","dnes musím pracovat","dnes MOO-seem PRAH-tso-vat"],["you must not run","nesmíš běhat","NEH-smeesh BYEH-hat"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Czech uses small words, and the noun changes its ending after them: v (in), na (on), u (at, by), do (to, into), z (from), s (with), pod (under)."],"rows":[["in","v","v"],["on","na","nah"],["at / by","u","oo"],["to / into","do","do"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kniha je na stole","KNYI-hah yeh nah STO-leh"],["the cat is under the table","kočka je pod stolem","KOCH-kah yeh pod STO-lem"],["I am at school","jsem ve škole","yem veh SHKO-leh"],["I am at home","jsem doma","yem DO-mah"],["the shop is next to the bank","obchod je vedle banky","OP-khot yeh VED-leh BAN-ki"],["the park is near the station","park je blízko nádraží","park yeh BLEES-ko NAH-drah-zhee"],["we meet in the morning","sejdeme se ráno","SEY-deh-meh seh RAH-no"],["the lesson is at nine","hodina je v devět","HO-dyi-nah yeh v DEH-vyet"],["the key is in the bag","klíč je v tašce","kleech yeh f TASH-tseh"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -ější / -ší for \"more\": velký, větší (irregular). For \"the most\" put \"nej-\" in front: největší. \"Than\" is \"než\"."],"rows":[["big, bigger, the biggest","velký, větší, největší"],["small, smaller, the smallest","malý, menší, nejmenší"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","velký, větší, největší","VEL-kee VYET-shee NEY-vyet-shee"],["small, smaller, the smallest","malý, menší, nejmenší","MAH-lee MEN-shee NEY-men-shee"],["this is better than that","tohle je lepší než tamto","TOH-leh yeh LEP-shee nezh TAM-to"],["this is worse than that","tohle je horší než tamto","TOH-leh yeh HOR-shee nezh TAM-to"],["she is taller than me","je vyšší než já","yeh VISH-shee nezh yah"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taškent je větší než Samarkand","TASH-kent yeh VYET-shee nezh SAH-mar-kant"],["it is the cheapest","je to nejlevnější","yeh to NEY-lev-nyeh-yshee"],["the same as","stejný jako","STEY-nee YAH-ko"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","je učitel","yeh OO-chi-tel"],["you (plural) are students","jste studenti","yste STOO-den-tyi"],["I am happy","jsem šťastný","yem SHTYAST-nee"],["she is at school","je ve škole","yeh veh SHKO-leh"],["you are my friend","jsi můj přítel","ysi mooy PRZHEE-tel"],["it is cold","je zima","yeh ZI-mah"],["I study English","studuji angličtinu","STOO-doo-yi AN-glich-tyi-noo"],["he teaches maths","učí matematiku","OO-chee MAH-teh-mah-ti-koo"],["they work every day","pracují každý den","PRAH-tsoo-yee KAZH-dee den"],["is this your book?","je to vaše kniha?","yeh to VAH-sheh KNYI-hah"],["are they here?","jsou tady?","ysoh TAH-di"],["do you like tea?","máte rádi čaj?","MAH-teh RAH-dyi chay"],["what time is it?","kolik je hodin?","KO-lik yeh HO-dyin"],["whose book is this?","čí je to kniha?","chee yeh to KNYI-hah"],["how old are you?","kolik ti je let?","KO-lik tyi yeh let"],["how do you say it?","jak se to řekne?","yak seh to RZHEK-neh"],["your book (formal)","vaše kniha","VAH-sheh KNYI-hah"],["their house","jejich dům","YEH-yikh doom"],["my phone","můj telefon","mooy TEH-leh-fon"],["excuse me, sir","promiňte, pane","PRO-min-yte, PAH-neh"],["please sit down (formal)","posaďte se, prosím","PO-sad-yte seh, PRO-seem"],["come here (informal)","pojď sem","poyty sem"],["yesterday I was tired","včera jsem byl unavený","FCHE-rah yem bil OO-nah-veh-nee"],["I will study tomorrow","zítra budu studovat","ZEE-trah BOO-doo STOO-do-vat"],["we went to the park","šli jsme do parku","shli ysmeh do PAR-koo"]]}],"name":"Czech","id":"cs","flag":"cz","note":""}